1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,540
Your workout took an hour.

2
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:03,330
But where did that hour go?

3
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:06,050
An hour in the gym
is not an hour of lifting.

4
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:08,980
In this made-up example:
fifteen minutes lifting.

5
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:11,300
Twenty-five resting.
Eight setting up.

6
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:12,580
And twelve waiting.

7
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:14,340
Those are four different problems.

8
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:16,690
Start with a delay you can
actually change.

9
00:00:16,847 --> 00:00:18,877
Like repeated trips for equipment.

10
00:00:18,927 --> 00:00:20,607
A time audit is not a reason

11
00:00:20,607 --> 00:00:22,287
to rush every rest period.

12
00:00:22,287 --> 00:00:25,277
The biggest block is not
automatically the problem.

13
00:00:25,327 --> 00:00:27,807
For one session,
log the four buckets.

14
00:00:27,807 --> 00:00:29,487
Make one practical change.

15
00:00:29,487 --> 00:00:31,117
Then compare the next session.

16
00:00:31,117 --> 00:00:33,567
Measure the friction
before you rewrite the plan.

17
00:00:33,567 --> 00:00:35,633
Know why. Train better.
